A||||12||KnightRyder31||Removel of air restrictor(in air intake)||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||01-29-2001||10:44 PM||||I want to remove the air restrictor in my fiero(84). How would I go about doing this?<BR>I tried to do it earlier, but the damn thing was to hard to pry off! What will this do for my car? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-29-2001||11:11 PM||||The air resrticter helps keep water from getting up to the air filter and intake.  With it out, the sound is a little "better", but I don't believe it adds too much to the overall performance.||||reg||3
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||01-29-2001||11:22 PM||||I agree, there is no real increase in power (not that shows on dynos or in person), but I love the sound without it, kinda like a jet engine or something.  Just get a baseball bat and bash that baby in (carefully of course)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Later,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Cooter||01-29-2001||11:44 PM||||I used a die grinder to cut mine out on the 4 cyl SE. Just more noise and no noticeable increase in performance. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SloPonti||01-29-2001||11:48 PM||||i took mine completly out-the whole air box inside the rear drivers side wheel well! i them made my own tube to replace it out of 3 inch pvc pipe! sounds great-no water problems-great ram air!!<BR>hope this helps!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ralfy9862||01-30-2001||09:23 AM||||How exactly do you remove that i took aprt the air intake thingy and i cant fin the restrictor i can reach part of my arm down the bottom of where it meats the filter. Do you remove it through that grate thing on the outside quarter panel?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||01-30-2001||11:01 AM||||If you had a scoop and then you replaced the baffle with some sort of pipe, you would gain some horsepower at high speed.  I think I'm going to make a fiberglass elbow to replace the air restricter.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MikeSchaefer||01-30-2001||08:42 PM||||Take off the side vent (black thing on side of car) and there will be like a plastic panel right there with a little hole on the bottom of it, that's the "restrictor" plate.  I bashed mine in with a baseball bat, but I was in a hurry.  Just get it out however you want.<BR>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000008||RaeQwan||01-30-2001||09:53 PM||||that thingie is one thing Pontiac got right, removing it doesn't add any performance.. atleast thats what some website said, some bigname website..<P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/dearabu/" TARGET=_blank>Dear Abu</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||KnightRyder31||01-30-2001||10:32 PM||||I got the damn thing out!!!<BR>I knocked the stupid thing out with a hammer and screw driver.||||reg||1
Z||000010||beer_stud_21||01-30-2001||11:06 PM||||Just went to West coast fieros website and look what i found for $45.00... Its "The Velocity Tube"  Check it out at <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||SloPonti||01-31-2001||12:14 AM||||that velocity tube thing is exactly what i made! except it only cost me about 6 bucks and it is 3 inches!! just use 3 inch pvc tube-no one sees it-the inner fender covers it! trust me it works!!!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||01-31-2001||12:09 PM||||I did the ram air thing too. took out the baffle and ran a piece of flex tube from scoop in side of a Ferrari 308 rebody. I dont know if its faster but sounds cool in summer with window down, sucking air right behind my head. In the rain works fine too, in fact its cheap water injection, a fine mist of water in fuel/air mixture is good. planes used to use it to boost HP.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
